 "How long does it take a child to form a habit?": 1,
 "It varies by child and task, usually a few weeks of daily repetition. Fixed timing and prompt encouragement matter more than a day count; when your child starts without a reminder, add the next task.": 1,
 "Will rewards make my child do it only for the reward?": 1,
 "What matters is that rewards are prompt, tied to a specific action and paired with specific praise. As the action becomes routine you can reduce prompts so finishing becomes the achievement itself.": 1,
 "What age is right to start habit missions?": 1,
 "Around three, children can follow the rule \"finish a step, tap once\". Lumi Mission Planet is a tool for parents, designed to be used together with children aged three to seven.": 1,
